 │ • Summary-only Findings: 1 unverified findings (needs context, omitted from inline)            │
 │                                                                                                │
 ╰────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

 Proposed review summary:
 Run: run-20261016-demo42 | Review status: ready
 Completed review of PR #42 across 4 canonical specialists. Found 2 verified P1 issues, 1 verified
 P2 issue, 1 requiring context, and 1 candidate rejected outside diff. Automated publishing is
 gated on operator dry-run review.
 worker-sec: complete
 worker-log: complete
 worker-arc: complete
 worker-qty: complete
 Tests were not executed directly by specialist workers (tests.executed=false)
 Findings based on AST diff heuristic simulation [DEMO ONLY]

 Summary only — needs context: [P2] Missing connection timeout on Redis client pool initialization
 Path: src/db/redis.ts:24 (RIGHT)
 Evidence: Redis client initialized without explicit connectTimeout or retryStrategy limits.
 Impact: Worker threads may hang indefinitely during network partitions or cloud provider socket
 resets.
 Recommendation: Configure connectTimeout: 3000ms and maxRetriesPerRequest: 3.


 Proposed inline comments:

 [P1] Null input is dereferenced in token resolver
 Path: src/demo.ts:17 (RIGHT)
 Evidence: parseToken(header) can return null when header is absent, but token.sub is dereferenced
 without guard.
 Impact: Unauthenticated or malformed requests will trigger unhandled TypeError 500 crashes.
 Recommendation: Add early null check: \`if (!token) return [];\` before accessing \`token.sub\`.


 [P1] Insecure fallback key generated when AUTH_SECRET is omitted
 Path: src/auth/token.ts:45 (RIGHT)
 Evidence: Generates static predictable token 'insecure-dev-fallback-key-' when env var is
 undefined.
 Impact: Attackers can forge arbitrary session credentials in environments with misconfigured
 secrets.
 Recommendation: Throw fatal initialization error if AUTH_SECRET is missing rather than falling
 back to static string.


 [P2] Unbounded in-memory Map leads to potential node memory leak
 Path: src/auth/session.ts:89 (RIGHT)
 Evidence: sessionStore is a global Map with no LRU eviction, size bounds, or TTL cleanup
 mechanism.
 Impact: Server process will experience continuous heap expansion and crash via OOM under sustained
  traffic.
 Recommendation: Implement an LRU cache with max capacity (e.g., lru-cache) or offload session
 storage to Redis with TTL.


 ╔════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
 ║                                                                                                ║
 ║ ✗ PUBLICATION DENIED BY OPERATOR                                                               ║
 ║ Review submission aborted. Report remains available in the current session.                    ║
 ║                                                                                                ║
 ╚════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

 Decision locked. Press [R] to Restart Demo | [Esc] Back"
`;

