 [P1] Null input is dereferenced in token resolver
 Path: src/demo.ts:17 (RIGHT)
 Evidence: parseToken(header) can return null when header is absent, but token.sub is dereferenced
 without guard.
 Impact: Unauthenticated or malformed requests will trigger unhandled TypeError 500 crashes.
 Recommendation: Add early null check: \`if (!token) return [];\` before accessing \`token.sub\`.


 [P1] Insecure fallback key generated when AUTH_SECRET is omitted
 Path: src/auth/token.ts:45 (RIGHT)
 Evidence: Generates static predictable token 'insecure-dev-fallback-key-' when env var is
 undefined.
 Impact: Attackers can forge arbitrary session credentials in environments with misconfigured
 secrets.
 Recommendation: Throw fatal initialization error if AUTH_SECRET is missing rather than falling
 back to static string.


 [P2] Unbounded in-memory Map leads to potential node memory leak
 Path: src/auth/session.ts:89 (RIGHT)
 Evidence: sessionStore is a global Map with no LRU eviction, size bounds, or TTL cleanup
 mechanism.
 Impact: Server process will experience continuous heap expansion and crash via OOM under sustained
  traffic.
 Recommendation: Implement an LRU cache with max capacity (e.g., lru-cache) or offload session
 storage to Redis with TTL.


